  "body": "(See also https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-doc/issues/2119).\r\n\r\nThere are some quite small changes we should make to the spec style to make it more readable and align it better with the [style guide](https://matrix-org.webflow.io/style-guide). This includes:\r\n\r\n* `font-weight: 400` for body text\r\n* `color: matrix-org/matrix-spec-proposals#333` for all text, including headings\r\n* `background-color: #F4F4F4` for ToC, headings, admonition boxes, and table headings\r\n\r\nThis would give us something like:\r\n\r\n********\r\n\r\n<img width=\"966\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2020-10-06 at 1 29 47 PM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/432915/95256791-25984a80-07d8-11eb-8e6c-ac1315098ffe.png\">\r\n\r\n\r\n********\r\n\r\n...rather than the current:\r\n\r\n********\r\n\r\n<img width=\"975\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2020-10-06 at 1 29 10 PM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/432915/95256750-13b6a780-07d8-11eb-969b-d1ce9e9810b8.png\">\r\n\r\n*******\r\n\r\nDoes this look like what we want? We could decide to keep more different background colors, although personally I like the more minimal look.\r\n\r\nAre there any other changes we might want to make at the same time?\r\n\r\nOne issue is that some of these styles are coming from the overall site CSS (in particular /docs/css/main.css and /docs/guides/css/docs_overrides.css) and they don't live inside matrix-doc. I'm not sure whether it would be better to override them in matrix-doc's CSS, or to change the site CSS.\r\n",
